    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1235">

                <pb facs="1058" n="954" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg954"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 412.00/30.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Chargé d’Affaires.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1447.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-10-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 15, 1913</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 2081,
                    of October 1, enclosing a translation of the minutes of a meeting between the
                    Sub-secretary for Foreign Affairs and certain members of the Diplomatic Corps,
                    to consider the creation of a commission for the settlement of the claims of
                    foreigners against Mexico, growing out of the disorders in that country.</p>
                <p>The enclosure to your despatch has been read with interest, and you are requested
                    to keep the Department fully informed of any further developments.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Moore</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
